<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<full-backup-content>
    <!--
      Set lists and settings are worth carrying to a new phone. Two things
      deliberately are not.

      The chart cache, because every file in it can be fetched again from the
      folder it came from, and a songbook of scans is not something to push
      through a backup.

      The library index, because it is a list of provider URIs, and a URI
      granted to one install means nothing to another. Restoring it would give
      the user a library full of entries that look right and will not open,
      which is worse than an empty one saying "add a folder".
    -->
    <include domain="file" path="setlists/" />
    <include domain="file" path="settings.json" />
</full-backup-content>
